(The local docs and scripts expect at least numpy, open3d, and kiss-icp for the SLAM path.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. SDK Wrapper Behavior) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SDK 2: livox2_python.py) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Prefers liblivox_lidar_sdk_shared.so or liblivox_lidar_sdk.so.) Tj
T*
(- Accepts overrides through LIVOX_SDK2_LIB or LIVOX_SDK2_DIR.) Tj
T*
(- Initializes the SDK with a JSON config path and host IP.) Tj
T*
(- Registers a point-cloud callback before starting SDK threads.) Tj
T*
(- On info-change, forces normal work mode, enables point sending, and selects Cartesian) Tj
T*
(  high point data.) Tj
T*
(- Aggregates many UDP packets into pseudo-frames before calling handle_points\(\).) Tj
T*
(Aggregation defaults in the wrapper constructor:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(frame_time=0.20) Tj
T*
(frame_packets=120) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Supported packet types currently handled in this wrapper:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- data_type == 1: Cartesian High, converted from millimeters to meters.) Tj
T*
(- data_type == 2: Cartesian Low, converted from centimeters to meters.) Tj
T*
(SDK 1: livox_python.py) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Searches for liblivox_sdk.so or LivoxSdk.dll.) Tj
T*
(- Supports overrides through LIVOX_SDK_LIB and LIVOX_SDK_DIR.) Tj
T*
(- Uses broadcast discovery and device-state callbacks.) Tj
T*
(- Connects to every detected LiDAR on the subnet and starts sampling.) Tj
T*
(- Forwards Cartesian packet formats to handle_points\(\) as float32 XYZ meters.) Tj
T*
(6. MID-360 JSON Configuration) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The repo ships a minimal sample at scripts/navigation/slam/mid360_config.json. It points) Tj
T*
(the host side to 192.168.123.222 and uses the standard MID-360 port layout.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
({) Tj
T*
("MID360": {) Tj
T*
("lidar_net_info": {) Tj
T*
("cmd_data_port": 56100,) Tj
ET
endstream
